Workflow: Task Execution

Purpose:
  Define how AI executes tasks from .sdd/project/.
  Tasks are derived from approved docs and .sdd/project/ structure.

Inputs:
  - .sdd/projects/vkard.az/tasks/*.sdd (task definitions)
  - .sdd/project/domains.sdd (domain structure)
  - .sdd/projects/vkard.az/stack/*.sdd (tech stack)
  - .sdd/skills/**/*.sdd (skill catalog)
  - .sdd/chains/*.sdd (execution chains)

Outputs:
  - Implemented code
  - Tests
  - Documentation
  - Updated task status

Steps:
  1. DISCOVER_TASKS:
     - Read .sdd/projects/vkard.az/tasks/INDEX.sdd
     - Find tasks with status: ready
     - Respect dependency order

  2. RESOLVE_CONTEXT:
     - Load task definition
     - Load relevant skills
     - Load domain model
     - Load tech stack

  3. SELECT_CHAIN:
     - Determine chain type (default/feature/bugfix/hotfix)
     - Load chain definition
     - Execute stages in order

  4. EXECUTE_STAGES:
     - For each stage in chain:
       - Load stage skill
       - Execute stage logic
       - Validate output
       - Update state

  5. VALIDATE:
     - Run tests
     - Run linter
     - Verify against .sdd/project/

  6. UPDATE_STATE:
     - Mark task complete
     - Update .sdd/project/state/
     - Notify human

Human Gates:
  - Plan review (before implementation)
  - Code review (after implementation)
  - Deployment approval (before production)

Rules:
  [TE1] Tasks MUST be executed in dependency order.
  [TE2] Each task MUST validate before proceeding.
  [TE3] Human MUST approve before production deployment.
  [TE4] All changes MUST be tracked in .sdd/project/state/.
  [TE5] Failed tasks MUST trigger recovery workflow.

State: +
